---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const tools = [
  {
    name: 'Daily Digest Engine',
    status: 'Live',
    desc: 'Reads a curated set of news feeds and search queries each morning, ranks and summarises what matters to my work, verifies the facts behind its recommendations, and emails a short brief with next actions. Runs on a self-hosted n8n instance.',
  },
  {
    name: 'FileMaker MCP server',
    status: 'In progress',
    desc: 'A Model Context Protocol server that lets AI coding agents inspect and work with FileMaker solutions safely.',
  },
];

const principles = [
  'I build and operate these tools myself, on my own infrastructure.',
  'They are personal tools: I am the operator and, in most cases, the only user.',
  'Where a tool connects to a third-party service, it requests the minimum access it needs and nothing more.',
  'No data handled by these tools is sold, shared, or used to train anything.',
];
---

<Layout title="Automation & Integrations - Jim Paul De Jose">
  <h1>Automation &amp; Integrations</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Personal automation and integration tools I build and run on my own self-hosted infrastructure.
  </p>

  <p>
    I build these to solve my own daily problems and to stay sharp on self-hosted, AI-assisted
    workflows. They are not public services: I am the operator and, in most cases, the only user.
    Some of them connect to third-party APIs, including Google services, to do their work.
  </p>

  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    {
      tools.map((tool) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{tool.name}</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>{tool.status}</strong>
          </p>
          <p>{tool.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    {principles.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Permissions and data</h2>
  <p>
    When one of these tools connects to an external service, it requests the minimum access it
    needs to do that job. The exact permissions being requested are shown on the service's
    authorisation screen at the moment you grant them.
  </p>
  <p>
    For tools that connect to Google services, how data is accessed, used, stored and shared is
    described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. The terms these tools are provided
    under are in the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
